      "topic": "Advanced algebra and functions",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "questionText": "The polynomial p(x) = x³ − 4x² − x + 4 has factor x − 1. What is its complete factorization?",
      "questionType": "multiple_choice",
      "options": [
        "(x − 1)(x − 2)²",
        "(x + 1)(x − 4)²",
        "(x − 1)(x² − 4)",
        "(x − 1)(x − 4)(x + 1)"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "(x − 1)(x − 4)(x + 1)",
      "explanation": "Factoring by grouping gives x²(x−4)−1(x−4) = (x²−1)(x−4) = (x−1)(x+1)(x−4).",
